From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:35:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: add a stateful JPEG decoder for the
 A10/A20 VE

The A10/A20 video engine decodes baseline JPEG on its MPEG engine. Add
it as a third video node, cedrus-jpeg, with the stateful decoder API of
dev-decoder.rst: there is no stateless JPEG uAPI and every other JPEG
decoder in the tree is stateful.

- OUTPUT takes V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG or MJPEG, one frame per buffer, MMAP or
  DMABUF. The kernel parses each header through its own mapping,
  bracketed by dma_buf_begin/end_cpu_access() for imported buffers.
- CAPTURE gives MB32-tiled pictures: V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_32L32 for 4:2:0
  and a new driver-private V4L2_PIX_FMT_CEDRUS_NV16_32L32 ('ST16',
  uapi/cedrus-dec.h) for 4:2:2, the format UVC cameras send, and for
  4:4:4, whose chroma the VE halves horizontally by averaging column
  pairs. The display engine scans both out directly; the VE has no
  linear JPEG output.
- Accepted: 8-bit baseline/extended sequential 4:2:0, 4:2:2 (h2v1) and
  4:4:4 in one interleaved scan, restart intervals, 16x16 to 4096x4096.
  Rejected: other samplings (the VE decodes 4:1:1 into a layout of its
  own and leaves the buffer untouched for gray), different Cb/Cr
  tables, oversubscribed or oversized Huffman tables, and scans that do
  not end with EOI (the VE then waits for more data and never
  finishes). Such frames and VE errors complete with
  V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR; a VE error resets the VE.
- The first valid frame sets the picture format and raises
  V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE; frames that are broken before it come back
  at once, so a client is never stuck behind a camera's start-up
  garbage.
- Dynamic resolution change without losing frames: the job parses the
  header again (an MMAP buffer can be rewritten after QBUF) and copies
  every table the VE uses before the first register write. A valid
  frame of another size or chroma layout is held in the queue: every
  earlier frame has completed by then, the next CAPTURE buffer goes back
  empty with LAST, the event announces the new format, and decoding
  resumes after CAPTURE STREAMOFF/STREAMON or V4L2_DEC_CMD_START (which
  refuses buffers too small for the new format). A drain requested
  before or during the change still ends with LAST and EOS; an OUTPUT
  restart drops a pending change.
- The JPEG watchdog scales with the frame: 500 ms plus ~2 us per block
  and ~61 ns per byte, 2.5x the slowest frames measured.
- Drain (DEC_CMD_STOP, LAST, EOS), sequence numbers on both queues and
  the compose rectangle follow dev-decoder.rst. V4L2_DEC_CMD_START now
  also schedules the frames queued while the decoder was stopped.

The TRIGGER register is written byte by byte, as the Allwinner library
does: a single 32-bit write decodes garbage. Buffers of one page or less
bypass the CMA pool on this platform and may land outside the VE's DMA
window, so picture buffers are at least two pages.

Decoded pictures match libjpeg's ISLOW raw planes within 1 (PSNR >= 61
dB) on 49 test images from 16x16 to 4096x4096, with restart intervals
from 1 to 65535; a 1024x768 4:2:2 frame takes 16 ms. A JPEG cut short
with an EOI appended still decodes "successfully" (the VE runs through
the missing MCUs), so damaged camera frames must also be caught by the
UVC error flag.

Tested on a Cubietruck (A20) and a Rikomagic MK802 (A10).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
